<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tapa Chermoev</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1882–1937</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tapa Chermoev (1882–1937) was a Chechen landowner, oil industrialist and former officer of the Russian imperial guard. In 1917–1918 he led the Union of the Peoples of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-caucasus">North Caucasus</a> and became the first head of government of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mountainous-republic-of-the-northern-caucasus">Mountainous Republic of the Northern Caucasus</a>. After the republic's collapse he spent the rest of his life in exile in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tapa-chermoev.jpg" alt="Tapa Chermoev" width="250" height="344" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown, irrelevant due to age · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tapa_Chermoyev.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
